  "description": "A high-density functional near-infrared spectroscopy (fNIRS) dataset recorded during a ball-squeezing motor task at Boston University. The recordings were used to develop and optimize surface-based image reconstruction methods for high-density fNIRS. The dataset is mirrored on NEMAR from OpenNeuro (ds006673).",
